id: CTB-SRC0033-rules
source: SRC-0033
section: §1.1
kind: requirement
scope: ARC
title: Every constitutional rule carries a check and an enforcement point
applied-in: STG-00.A-1
distinct-from: LXM-REQ-000091, LXM-REQ-000099, LXM-REQ-000170
text: The architecture constitution is a destination plus enforceable rules: every rule has an invariant (what must be true), a check (how a machine knows) and an enforcement point (where a violation is stopped). A rule without a check is a principle, not yet a rule.
